---
// PartnershipsContent.astro — Unified partnerships data room page content
---

<!-- Hero Section -->
<section class="partnerships-hero">
  <div class="partnerships-container">
    <div class="hero-content">
      <p class="hero-label">Partnerships</p>
      <h1 class="hero-title">Partner With Auditware</h1>
      <p class="hero-description">
        Everything partners, referrers, and comarketing collaborators need in one place — program details, product context, media assets, and resources.
      </p>
      <a href="https://calendly.com/d/cnqr-49f-xdy/auditware-consultation" class="hero-cta" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">
        Get in Touch
        <svg width="16" height="16" viewBox="0 0 16 16" fill="none" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg">
          <path d="M6 12L10 8L6 4" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/>
        </svg>
      </a>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- Sticky Section Navigation -->
<nav class="section-nav" id="sectionNav">
  <div class="section-nav-inner">
    <a href="#overview" class="section-nav-link active" data-section="overview">Overview</a>
    <a href="#referral" class="section-nav-link" data-section="referral">Referral Program</a>
    <a href="#sentry" class="section-nav-link" data-section="sentry">Sentry</a>
    <a href="#resources" class="section-nav-link" data-section="resources">Resources</a>
    <a href="#media-assets" class="section-nav-link" data-section="media-assets">Media Assets</a>
  </div>
</nav>

<!-- Section 1: Partnership Overview -->
<section class="partnerships-section" id="overview">
  <div class="partnerships-container">
    <div class="section-header">
      <h2 class="section-title">Partnership Overview</h2>
    </div>

    <!-- The Problem -->
    <div class="content-block">
      <h3 class="content-subtitle">The Problem</h3>
      <p class="content-text">
        Every Web3 team has operational risk. The most common failures start with leaked keys, malware infections, and access control failures — not just smart contracts. Everyone is attacked eventually. Teams that take OpSec seriously early are the ones that survive those attacks.
      </p>
    </div>

    <!-- What We Offer -->
    <div class="content-block">
      <h3 class="content-subtitle">What We Offer</h3>
      <div class="offerings-grid">
        <div class="offering-card">
          <div class="offering-icon">
            <svg width="24" height="24" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round">
              <path d="M12 22s8-4 8-10V5l-8-3-8 3v7c0 6 8 10 8 10z"/>
            </svg>
          </div>
          <h4 class="offering-title">OpSec Audits</h4>
          <p class="offering-desc">Covering people, communications, endpoints, and response readiness.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="offering-card">
          <div class="offering-icon">
            <svg width="24" height="24" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round">
              <path d="M1 12s4-8 11-8 11 8 11 8-4 8-11 8-11-8-11-8z"/><circle cx="12" cy="12" r="3"/>
            </svg>
          </div>
          <h4 class="offering-title">Sentry Monitoring</h4>
          <p class="offering-desc">Continuous threat visibility and compliance tracking platform.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="offering-card">
          <div class="offering-icon">
            <svg width="24" height="24" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round">
              <polyline points="16 18 22 12 16 6"/><polyline points="8 6 2 12 8 18"/>
            </svg>
          </div>
          <h4 class="offering-title">Smart Contract & Protocol Audits</h4>
          <p class="offering-desc">For EVM and Rust-based systems with custom static analysis.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="offering-card">
          <div class="offering-icon">
            <svg width="24" height="24" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round">
              <rect x="2" y="3" width="20" height="14" rx="2" ry="2"/><line x1="8" y1="21" x2="16" y2="21"/><line x1="12" y1="17" x2="12" y2="21"/>
            </svg>
          </div>
          <h4 class="offering-title">App & Infrastructure Audits</h4>
          <p class="offering-desc">Web2 code, cloud environments, and CI/CD pipelines.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
      <p class="content-note">Teams typically start with OpSec, then expand into audits, monitoring, and retainers as they mature.</p>
    </div>

    <!-- Why Auditware -->
    <div class="content-block why-block">
      <h3 class="content-subtitle">Why Auditware</h3>
      <p class="content-text">
        Auditware is building the OpSec layer Web3 is missing. We combine the security standard, platform, and execution into one coherent security workflow:
      </p>
      <div class="why-items">
        <div class="why-item">
          <span class="why-label">W3OS</span>
          <span class="why-desc">The open-source Web3 Operational Security Standard</span>
        </div>
        <div class="why-item">
          <span class="why-label">Sentry</span>
          <span class="why-desc">Continuous OpSec tracking and monitoring platform</span>
        </div>
        <div class="why-item">
          <span class="why-label">Hands-on Audits</span>
          <span class="why-desc">Across operations, infrastructure, Web2, and smart contracts</span>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- Section 2: Referral Program -->
<section class="partnerships-section" id="referral">
  <div class="partnerships-container">
    <div class="section-header">
      <h2 class="section-title">Referral Program</h2>
    </div>

    <!-- Referral Incentives -->
    <div class="referral-stats">
      <div class="referral-stat">
        <span class="stat-value">10%</span>
        <span class="stat-label">Revenue share on accepted OpSec audits and security engagements</span>
      </div>
      <div class="referral-stat">
        <span class="stat-value">6 months</span>
        <span class="stat-label">Retainer revenue included for referred clients</span>
      </div>
      <div class="referral-stat">
        <span class="stat-value">Custom</span>
        <span class="stat-label">Terms available for long-term collaborators</span>
      </div>
    </div>

    <!-- How Engagements Work -->
    <div class="content-block">
      <h3 class="content-subtitle">How Engagements Work</h3>
      <div class="engagement-steps">
        <div class="engagement-step">
          <span class="step-number">1</span>
          <div class="step-content">
            <h4 class="step-title">Direct CEO Involvement</h4>
            <p class="step-desc">Scoping, review, and execution all involve direct leadership.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="engagement-step">
          <span class="step-number">2</span>
          <div class="step-content">
            <h4 class="step-title">OpSec Engagement</h4>
            <p class="step-desc">Sentry onboarding, W3OS-aligned operational audit, team training, and remediation support.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="engagement-step">
          <span class="step-number">3</span>
          <div class="step-content">
            <h4 class="step-title">Ongoing Coverage</h4>
            <p class="step-desc">Continues via Sentry (freemium entry available), retainers, and follow-on audits as teams mature.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- Section 3: Sentry Product Context (Comarketing) -->
<section class="partnerships-section" id="sentry">
  <div class="partnerships-container">
    <div class="section-header">
      <h2 class="section-title">Sentry — Product Context</h2>
      <p class="section-description">Comarketing information for partners communicating about Sentry.</p>
    </div>

    <!-- What is Sentry -->
    <div class="content-block">
      <h3 class="content-subtitle">What is Sentry</h3>
      <p class="content-text">
        Sentry is a <strong>free operational security platform</strong> built from how Auditware evaluates teams during real security audits. It provides continuous OpSec monitoring and tracking against the Web3 Operational Security Standard (W3OS) in areas that sit outside code audits. Sentry addresses the human security risk — securing more than just code.
      </p>
    </div>

    <!-- Why It Matters -->
    <div class="content-block">
      <h3 class="content-subtitle">Why It Matters</h3>
      <ul class="styled-list">
        <li>Beyond point-in-time audits, operational risk evolves continuously</li>
        <li>Most security failures originate from people, access, and operational processes</li>
        <li>Teams lack visibility into these risks, and scaling best practices to their team</li>
      </ul>
    </div>

    <!-- Who It's For -->
    <div class="content-block">
      <h3 class="content-subtitle">Who It's For</h3>
      <div class="audience-pills">
        <span class="pill">Web3 Projects</span>
        <span class="pill">Web2.5 Teams</span>
        <span class="pill">Investors / HNWIs</span>
        <span class="pill">Startups</span>
        <span class="pill">Mature Organizations</span>
      </div>
    </div>

    <!-- What Sentry Includes -->
    <div class="content-block">
      <h3 class="content-subtitle">What Sentry Includes</h3>
      <div class="feature-cards">
        <div class="feature-card">
          <h4 class="feature-card-title">W3OS-Compliant Review</h4>
          <p class="feature-card-desc">Operational review across people, communications, endpoints, access, and response readiness.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="feature-card">
          <h4 class="feature-card-title">Continuous Monitoring</h4>
          <p class="feature-card-desc">Domain risk, credential leakage, and repository compromise signal detection.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="feature-card">
          <h4 class="feature-card-title">Remediation Guidance</h4>
          <p class="feature-card-desc">Operational guidance grounded in real audit findings and security incidents.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <!-- How Teams Use It -->
    <div class="content-block">
      <h3 class="content-subtitle">How Teams Use Sentry</h3>
      <div class="usage-steps">
        <div class="usage-step">
          <span class="usage-num">01</span>
          <p>Onboard with a structured W3OS self-review</p>
        </div>
        <div class="usage-step">
          <span class="usage-num">02</span>
          <p>Monitor and track operational posture over time</p>
        </div>
        <div class="usage-step">
          <span class="usage-num">03</span>
          <p>Prepare for audits and security tasks</p>
        </div>
        <div class="usage-step">
          <span class="usage-num">04</span>
          <p>Track progress between audits, monitoring, and remediation</p>
        </div>
      </div>
      <p class="content-note">Sentry is free to use. Paid audits and monitoring services are scoped separately.</p>
    </div>

    <!-- Ready-Made Copy -->
    <div class="content-block">
      <h3 class="content-subtitle">Ready-Made Copy</h3>
      <p class="content-text copy-intro">Use these descriptions when communicating about Sentry in your own channels.</p>

      <details class="accordion">
        <summary class="accordion-trigger">Social Media Copy</summary>
        <div class="accordion-content">
          <div class="copy-block">
            <p>"Sentry is a platform for continuously monitoring operational security for Web3 organizations. Built on W3OS and practical best practices, it provides ongoing visibility into OpSec risks that sit outside traditional code audits."</p>
          </div>
          <div class="copy-block">
            <p>"Sentry provides continuous OpSec monitoring for Web3 teams, covering W3OS compliance, credential exposure, domain risk, and repository compromise detection. It's free to use and designed to complement audits with ongoing operational visibility."</p>
          </div>
          <div class="copy-block">
            <p>"Sentry is Auditware's platform for continuous operational security monitoring, built from how teams are evaluated during real audits."</p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </details>

      <details class="accordion">
        <summary class="accordion-trigger">Newsletter Blurb</summary>
        <div class="accordion-content">
          <div class="copy-block">
            <p>Auditware has released <strong>Sentry</strong>, a platform for continuously monitoring operational security for Web3 organizations.</p>
            <p>Built on the open-source Web3 Operational Security Standard (W3OS), Sentry provides ongoing visibility into risks such as credential leakage, domain exposure, repository compromise, and team security posture.</p>
            <p>Sentry is free to use and designed to complement audits with continuous OpSec monitoring.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </details>
    </div>

    <!-- Key Links -->
    <div class="content-block">
      <h3 class="content-subtitle">Key Links</h3>
      <div class="link-buttons">
        <a href="https://sentry.auditware.io" class="link-btn" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">
          <svg width="16" height="16" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="M18 13v6a2 2 0 01-2 2H5a2 2 0 01-2-2V8a2 2 0 012-2h6"/><polyline points="15 3 21 3 21 9"/><line x1="10" y1="14" x2="21" y2="3"/></svg>
          Sentry Platform
        </a>
        <a href="https://docs.sentry.auditware.io/" class="link-btn" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">
          <svg width="16" height="16" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="M14 2H6a2 2 0 00-2 2v16a2 2 0 002 2h12a2 2 0 002-2V8z"/><polyline points="14 2 14 8 20 8"/><line x1="16" y1="13" x2="8" y2="13"/><line x1="16" y1="17" x2="8" y2="17"/></svg>
          Documentation
        </a>
        <a href="https://auditware.io/sentry" class="link-btn" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">
          <svg width="16" height="16" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><circle cx="12" cy="12" r="10"/><line x1="2" y1="12" x2="22" y2="12"/><path d="M12 2a15.3 15.3 0 014 10 15.3 15.3 0 01-4 10 15.3 15.3 0 01-4-10 15.3 15.3 0 014-10z"/></svg>
          Product Page
        </a>
        <a href="https://x.com/audit_wizard/status/2019848608577880169" class="link-btn" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">
          <svg width="16" height="16" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="M23 3a10.9 10.9 0 01-3.14 1.53 4.48 4.48 0 00-7.86 3v1A10.66 10.66 0 013 4s-4 9 5 13a11.64 11.64 0 01-7 2c9 5 20 0 20-11.5a4.5 4.5 0 00-.08-.83A7.72 7.72 0 0023 3z"/></svg>
          Launch Post
        </a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- Section 4: Resources — Product Deck (Embedded) -->
<section class="partnerships-section" id="resources">
  <div class="partnerships-container">
    <div class="section-header">
      <h2 class="section-title">Product Deck</h2>
      <p class="section-description">Our product information deck covering Auditware's services, platform, and positioning.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="deck-embed-wrapper">
      <div class="deck-embed-container">
        <iframe
          src="https://www.canva.com/design/DAG1CJP46v4/view?embed"
          allowfullscreen
          allow="fullscreen"
          loading="lazy"
          title="Auditware Product Deck"
        ></iframe>
      </div>
      <div class="deck-fallback">
        <a href="https://www.canva.com/design/DAG1CJP46v4/qQJg8ZtjbvIvLj4dOxhp_w/view" class="link-btn" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">
          <svg width="16" height="16" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="M18 13v6a2 2 0 01-2 2H5a2 2 0 01-2-2V8a2 2 0 012-2h6"/><polyline points="15 3 21 3 21 9"/><line x1="10" y1="14" x2="21" y2="3"/></svg>
          Open in Canva
        </a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- Section 5: Brand & Media Assets -->
<section class="partnerships-section" id="media-assets">
  <div class="partnerships-container">
    <div class="section-header">
      <h2 class="section-title">Brand & Media Assets</h2>
      <p class="section-description">Visual assets for referencing Auditware in your content or publications.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="assets-grid">
      <div class="asset-card">
        <div class="asset-preview">
          <img src="/images/tryagain.png" loading="lazy" width="300" alt="Auditware Main Logo" />
        </div>
        <p class="asset-label">Main logo — Light background</p>
      </div>
      <div class="asset-card">
        <div class="asset-preview">
          <img src="/images/Icon-black.png" loading="lazy" width="300" alt="Auditware Icon Logo" />
        </div>
        <p class="asset-label">Icon logo — Dark background</p>
      </div>
      <div class="asset-card">
        <div class="asset-preview">
          <img src="/images/Long-logo-dark.png" loading="lazy" width="454" alt="Auditware Long Logo Dark" />
        </div>
        <p class="asset-label">Long logo — Dark background</p>
      </div>
      <div class="asset-card">
        <div class="asset-preview">
          <img src="/images/Dark-longg.png" loading="lazy" width="442" alt="Auditware Long Logo Light" />
        </div>
        <p class="asset-label">Long logo — Light background</p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="assets-cta">
      <p class="content-text">Need additional formats or have proposals? <a href="https://calendly.com/d/cnqr-49f-xdy/auditware-consultation" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="inline-link">Get in touch</a>.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<style>
  /* ========================================
     Layout & Container
     ======================================== */
  .partnerships-container {
    max-width: var(--container-xl);
    margin: 0 auto;
    padding: 0 var(--spacing-6);
  }

  .partnerships-section {
    padding: var(--spacing-20) 0;
    position: relative;
  }

  .partnerships-section + .partnerships-section {
    border-top: 1px solid var(--color-border-primary);
  }

  /* ========================================
     Hero Section
     ======================================== */
  .partnerships-hero {
    padding: var(--spacing-24) 0 var(--spacing-16);
    text-align: center;
  }

  .hero-content {
    max-width: 720px;
    margin: 0 auto;
  }

  .hero-label {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: var(--font-size-sm);
    font-weight: var(--font-weight-medium);
    letter-spacing: var(--letter-spacing-widest);
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--color-primary-400);
    margin-bottom: var(--spacing-4);
  }

  .hero-title {
    font-size: var(--font-size-5xl);
    font-weight: var(--font-weight-bold);
    color: var(--color-text-primary);
    margin: 0 0 var(--spacing-6);
    line-height: var(--line-height-tight);
    background: linear-gradient(135deg, var(--color-text-primary) 0%, var(--color-primary-300) 100%);
    -webkit-background-clip: text;
    -webkit-text-fill-color: transparent;
    background-clip: text;
  }

  .hero-description {
    font-size: var(--font-size-lg);
    color: var(--color-text-secondary);
    line-height: var(--line-height-relaxed);
    margin: 0 0 var(--spacing-8);
  }

  .hero-cta {
    display: inline-flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: var(--spacing-2);
    padding: var(--spacing-4) var(--spacing-8);
    background: var(--gradient-primary);
    color: var(--color-text-primary);
    border: 1px solid rgba(var(--color-primary-500), 0.4);
    border-color: var(--color-border-purple);
    border-radius: var(--radius-full);
    font-size: var(--font-size-lg);
    font-weight: var(--font-weight-medium);
    text-decoration: none;
    transition: all var(--transition-base);
  }

  .hero-cta:hover {
    transform: translateY(-2px);
    box-shadow: var(--shadow-glow-medium);
  }

  .hero-cta:active {
    transform: translateY(0) scale(0.98);
  }

  .hero-cta svg {
    transition: transform var(--transition-base);
  }

  .hero-cta:hover svg {
    transform: translateX(2px);
  }

  /* ========================================
     Sticky Section Navigation
     ======================================== */
  .section-nav {
    position: sticky;
    top: 72px;
    z-index: var(--z-index-sticky);
    background: rgba(10, 10, 10, 0.8);
    backdrop-filter: blur(24px);
    -webkit-backdrop-filter: blur(24px);
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--color-border-primary);
    border-top: 1px solid var(--color-border-primary);
  }

  .section-nav-inner {
    max-width: var(--container-xl);
    margin: 0 auto;
    padding: 0 var(--spacing-6);
    display: flex;
    gap: var(--spacing-1);
    overflow-x: auto;
    -webkit-overflow-scrolling: touch;
    scrollbar-width: none;
  }

  .section-nav-inner::-webkit-scrollbar {
    display: none;
  }

  .section-nav-link {
    display: inline-flex;
    align-items: center;
    padding: var(--spacing-4) var(--spacing-5);
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: var(--font-size-sm);
    font-weight: var(--font-weight-medium);
    color: var(--color-text-muted);
    text-decoration: none;
    white-space: nowrap;
    border-bottom: 2px solid transparent;
    transition: all var(--transition-base);
  }

  .section-nav-link:hover {
    color: var(--color-text-secondary);
  }

  .section-nav-link.active {
    color: var(--color-primary-400);
    border-bottom-color: var(--color-primary-500);
  }

  /* ========================================
     Section Headers
     ======================================== */
  .section-header {
    margin-bottom: var(--spacing-12);
  }

  .section-title {
    font-size: var(--font-size-3xl);
    font-weight: var(--font-weight-bold);
    color: var(--color-text-primary);
    margin: 0 0 var(--spacing-3);
    line-height: var(--line-height-tight);
  }

  .section-description {
    font-size: var(--font-size-lg);
    color: var(--color-text-muted);
    margin: 0;
    line-height: var(--line-height-relaxed);
  }

  /* ========================================
     Content Blocks
     ======================================== */
  .content-block {
    margin-bottom: var(--spacing-12);
  }

  .content-block:last-child {
    margin-bottom: 0;
  }

  .content-subtitle {
    font-size: var(--font-size-xl);
    font-weight: var(--font-weight-semibold);
    color: var(--color-text-primary);
    margin: 0 0 var(--spacing-4);
  }

  .content-text {
    font-size: var(--font-size-base);
    color: var(--color-text-secondary);
    line-height: var(--line-height-relaxed);
    margin: 0;
    max-width: 720px;
  }

  .content-text strong {
    color: var(--color-text-primary);
    font-weight: var(--font-weight-semibold);
  }

  .content-note {
    font-size: var(--font-size-sm);
    color: var(--color-text-muted);
    margin-top: var(--spacing-6);
    font-style: italic;
  }

  .copy-intro {
    margin-bottom: var(--spacing-6);
  }

  /* ========================================
     Offerings Grid (2x2)
     ======================================== */
  .offerings-grid {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(2, 1fr);
    gap: var(--spacing-5);
    margin-top: var(--spacing-6);
  }

  .offering-card {
    background: var(--color-background-glass);
    border: 1px solid var(--color-border-primary);
    border-radius: var(--radius-xl);
    padding: var(--spacing-6);
    transition: all var(--transition-base);
  }

  .offering-card:hover {
    border-color: var(--color-border-purple);
